==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|tastelesse}} {{q|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|taste|less}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈteɪstləs/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-tasteless.wav|a=US}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{senseid|en|bland, unflavorful}} Having no [[flavour]]; [[bland]]; [[insipid]].
#: {{hyper|en|untasty}}
#: {{cot|en|distasteful}}
#: {{nearsyn|en|untasteable}}
#: {{ux|en|They accused the cook of being a hack, claiming that the soup was '''tasteless'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|crass, indelicate}} Lacking [[delicacy]], [[refinement]]{{,}} and good taste; [[unbecoming]]; [[crass]].
#: {{syn|en|untasteful|Thesaurus:gaudy}}
#: {{ant|en|tasteful}}
#: {{ux|en|They accused the designer of being a '''tasteless''' hack.}}
#: {{ux|en|That was a rather '''tasteless''' attack on the designer, especially given that many people like the design.}}

